---
config:
  theme: neutral
  layout: elk
  look: handDrawn
title: LIQUIDO - Polly
---
flowchart TB
    Create("<pre><b>/polly</b></pre> Enter a question and some options")
    --> Tap["Tap to confirm<br>(Face-ID / fingerprint / device PIN)"]
    --> Live(["Polly is live. Friends can vote right away."])
    Live --> Share["Share ONE link<br>(share sheet / QR / copy)"]

    Open("<pre><b>/polly/:publicId</b></pre> A friend opens the link")
    --> Known{{"Passkey recognised?"}}
    Known -- "no, first time" --> Register["Register passkey<br>(one tap)"] --> Sort
    Known -- yes --> Sort["Sort the options<br>favourite on top"]
    --> Voted(["Vote counted.<br>One per passkey."])

    Live --> Finish["Owner taps Finish"]
    --> Winner(["Winner by Ranked Pairs"])

    Owner("<pre><b>/polly</b></pre> Owner returns later")
    --> MyPollys["myPollys: everything this passkey created"]
    --> Live

     Tap:::UserInput
     Register:::UserInput
     Sort:::UserInput
     Known:::Decision
     Live:::Aqua
     Voted@{ shape: dbl-circ }
     Winner@{ shape: dbl-circ }
     Finish@{ shape: trap-t }
    classDef UserInput fill:#FFF,color:#333
    classDef Decision fill:#3F3,color:#333
    classDef Aqua stroke-width:1px, stroke-dasharray:none, stroke:#46EDC8, fill:#DEFFF8, color:#378E7A

%% Notes on the design
%%
%% ONE link. There is no separate admin link and nothing secret in the URL: a passkey is a
%% discoverable credential scoped to the domain, so whoever opens the link is identified by
%% their own device. The creator sees Edit/Finish, everybody else sees a ballot.
%%
%% NO email anywhere. The passkey is both the login and the bookmark - myPollys returns
%% everything this credential created.
%%
%% TWO states only: VOTING -> FINISHED. A polly is live from the moment it exists; there is
%% no elaboration phase and no start step.
%%
%% NO voterTokens. Those exist so a LIQUIDO team poll is *truly* anonymous. A polly instead
%% stores HMAC(serverSecret, credentialId + pollyId) with UNIQUE(polly_id, voter_key), which
%% gives one vote per passkey. That makes a polly ballot pseudonymous, not anonymous - the
%% right trade for "where shall we go for dinner", the wrong one for a real election.
